<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eight Deer Jaguar Claw</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1063">1063</a>–<a href="/years/1115">1115</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Lord Eight Deer</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eight Deer Jaguar Claw was a Mixtec ruler whose life is told in pictorial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a> such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/codex-zouche-nuttall">Codex Zouche-Nuttall</a>. Born into a noble family linked to Tilantongo, he established himself at Tututepec on the coast around 1083 and then won Tilantongo, uniting much of the Mixteca through conquest and marriage alliances. He was captured and sacrificed by his enemies in 1115.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eight-deer-jaguar-claw.jpg" alt="Eight Deer Jaguar Claw" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: An author from the Mixteca region c.1500 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Codex_Zouche-Nuttall_-_Lord_8_Deer_Lord_4_Jaguar.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
